WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.890
In this lesson, you will learn to explain how one character can send a message that starts another character’s script, and plan a relay.

2
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:13.910
The orange envelope block sends a message — like passing a note.

3
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:19.270
The yellow “start on message” block waits for that message, then runs.

4
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.440
Messages have colours.

5
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.030
A red message only starts scripts waiting for red.

6
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.200
Rabbit runs, then sends a message.

7
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.920
Turtle gets it and runs next.

8
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.410
Teamwork!

9
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.100
The rabbit runs to the turtle (star) and says “Your turn!” — that’s the message.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.580
Message passed — now the turtle can go!

11
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:46.200
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.610
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
